course: dictionary
lesson: 9408
title: One word, many meanings: square
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word square has many meanings, and the sentence around it tells you which one to use. «A triangle frame keeps its shape when pushed, but a square frame can be pushed out of shape.» Here square is a flat shape with four equal sides and four square corners.
explain: Look at the clues in «If the perimeter is 26 cm and the length is 8 cm, ... the area is 8 × 5 = 40 square centimetres.» Square is about measuring area, so it is a unit, not a shape. Ask yourself which meaning fits the words around it, then try that meaning in the sentence.
explain: Square can also be a verb: to square something means to multiply it by itself. Square can be a place too: «the town square» is an open space with buildings around it. In casual talk, «Don't be such a square» means a dull person who does not follow fashion.
explain: Some phrases use square in a special way. «Back to square one» means start again, and «fair and square» means honestly. You cannot guess these from the single word, so read the whole sentence before you decide.
fact: A square is a flat shape with four equal sides and four right angles.
fact: The square of a number is the number multiplied by itself: the square of 5 is 25.
fact: Square numbers include 1, 4, 9, 16 and 25.
fact: Square units measure area, such as square metres and square feet.
fact: «A square meal» is a good, full meal, and «all square» means even or equal.
exercise: «A triangle frame keeps its shape when pushed, but a square frame can be pushed out of shape.» What is a square? | A place with buildings around it | *A flat shape with four equal sides and four right angles | A round shape with no corners | A shape with three sides
exercise: What is the square of 5? | 15 | *25 | 10 | 5
exercise: «We're square now, so you owe me nothing.» What does «we're square» mean? | *We owe each other nothing | We have lost the game | We must fight each other | We are standing in a square shape
test: «If the perimeter is 26 cm and the length is 8 cm, the area is 8 × 5 = 40 square centimetres.» What does square mean in square centimetres? | *A unit that measures area | To pay what you owe | An open place in a town | To multiply something by itself
test: «Don't be such a square.» What does square mean here? | *A dull person who does not follow fashion | A flat shape with four equal sides | An open place in a town | A good, full meal
exam: In a maths exam, what do we call a number multiplied by itself? | A side | A unit | *A square | A perimeter
